I'm trying to figure something out:
The SQL standard requires that every column referenced in the SELECT list of a grouped query must either appear in the GROUP BY clause or be an argument to an aggregate function. A table named orders has columns customer_id and order_total. The following query is executed: SELECT customer_id, order_total FROM orders GROUP BY customer_id;

Which column in the SELECT list violates the stated SQL GROUP BY rule?

